  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have 1505 friends. It's not useful for me to have to scroll through all of the friends of mines that are in private worlds if I can't join on them anyway.\n\nIf I could just hide everyone who's in a Private World without Join Me Status, that would drastically lower the number of names I have to scroll through just while looking at who's online.\n\nAnd if I want to specifically hunt down random people in private worlds, it'd be easier if I could sort them to all be in a row.\n\nRecently Met sorting would allow you to sort based on ... how recently you last met someone. For example, you could find the person you haven't seen for the longest time much easier with this type of sort.\n\nThere's probably other good criteria for sorting and filtering friends. If you can think of any, please comment!",
